[339.657431, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[115D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[115C\u001b[3A.\r\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[116C\u001b[3A\u001b[?25h"]
[341.524805, "o", "\u001b]0;⠂ Claude Code\u0007"]
[341.530163, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[116D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[14A\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;239m❯ \u001b[38;5;231m/init This is a repository where I will be working on my CV. It is planned that:\u001b[39m                                                      \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- It will connect to my ORCID and manage publications, grants, employment, etc. keeping both records synchronized.\u001b[39m                      \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- It will keep a YAML database of all my publications, stratified by journal papers, oral presentations at conferences, poster \u001b[39m         \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mpresentations, invited talks, software contributions, registered reports at Stage 1, preprints, etc.\u001b[39m                                    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- Commit etiquette: follow the conventional commits guidelines, with a type (enh:, fix:, chore:, ..) at the beginning of the message. \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mKeep commit bodies as short as necessary,"]
[341.530191, "o", " and make sure you tag yourself as a co-author.\u001b[39m                                                \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- PR etiquette: all changes must be added to the repo through PRs. PRs use the conventional commit types for the title, but using \u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mALLCAPS. E.g.: `FIX: Correct publication date of ...`. PRs have less terse descriptions, although you still want to avoid \u001b[39m              \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231moverexplaining. When a PR closes an issue, do not forget to add the automation (e.g., `Fixes: #340`)\u001b[39m                                    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- The repository will have tooling to generate CV versions in PDF, that tooling requires tests and will use latex.\u001b[39m                      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m✢\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mScurryin\u001b[38;5;216mg…\u001b[38;5;174m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[38;5;244m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[341.530357, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;220m⏵⏵\u001b[6Gauto\u001b[11Gmode\u001b[16Gon\u001b[38;5;246m (shift+tab\u001b[30Gto\u001b[33Gcycle)\u001b[40G·\u001b[42Gesc\u001b[46Gto\u001b[49Ginterrupt\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?25h"]
[341.540983, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[8C\u001b[6A\u001b[38;5;216min\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;174m…\u001b[39m\r\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?25h"]
[341.58989, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[6A\u001b[38;5;174m✳\u001b[9Gi\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;216m…\u001b[39m\r\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?25h"]
[341.634903, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[9C\u001b[6A\u001b[38;5;174mn\u001b[39m\r\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?25h"]
